IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cpf-exemption`

-- Central Provident Fund (Exemption) Order 2018 (S 61/2018, as amended), made by the Minister for Manpower under s 69 of the
-- Central Provident Fund Act 1953 -- THE CURRENT VERSION: paragraphs 2, 3, 3A, 4 and 5 and the Schedule.
--
-- EDITION: 2025 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, version in force from 1 June 2026 (SSO's "current version as at
-- 13 Oct 2026"), deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/CPFA1953-OR10.txt. The version as made (in force 1 January to
-- 1 February 2018) is encoded separately in cpf-exemption.l4 from CPFA1953-S61-2018.txt, and is left as it was.
--
-- WHY. Added on 12 October 2026 for REQ-0265 (Haziq scenario, event rule-version check raised 11 Oct 2026): has the Order been
-- amended since it was made, and does any amendment change who is exempt, in particular students on approved training?
--
-- THE SCHEDULE HAS BEEN RENUMBERED. The deposit's Legislative History lists S 73/2018, S 716/2024 (two commencements),
-- S 1031/2024, the 2025 Revised Edition, S 895/2025 and S 325/2026. In the current text:
--   Sched para 1  [Deleted by S 325/2026]       (as made: domestic employee, 14 hours a week -- now Order para 4, transitional)
--   Sched para 2  UN employees                  (as made: para 2, reworded by S 895/2025)
--   Sched para 2A ICSID and MIGA employees      (new, S 895/2025)
--   Sched para 3  OECD staff at the IEA Regional Cooperation Centre   (as made: para 3 was the seamen -- now Order para 5)
--   Sched paras 4, 5 [Deleted by S 325/2026]    (what they said just before deletion is NOT in the deposit)
--   Sched para 6  students on approved training (as made: para 5)
--   Sched para 7  private education institution students (as made: para 6)
--   Sched para 8  overseas tertiary students    (as made: para 7)
--   Sched para 9  school pupils in the holidays (as made: para 8)
--   the as-made para 9 (SHATEC trainees) and para 4 (Seventh-Day Adventists) do not appear in the current text.
-- Which amendment moved which paragraph cannot be read from the deposit: the amending orders were not retrieved.
--
-- The student paragraphs (now 6 to 9) carry the same words as the as-made paragraphs 5 to 8, save for updated Act citations,
-- "student of" for "student in" in para 7(a), and the MOE web address. This module therefore REUSES the Student and Institution
-- types of cpf-exemption.l4; the Institution called `a school listed in paragraph 8` there is the school list now in para 9.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: para 1 (citation); which institutions fall within each paragraph, whether training is "approved by the
-- institution", whether someone is a "domestic employee" (para 4(4)), a "platform worker" or "seaman" -- all inputs; the
-- content of the community funds under s 76(3) of the Act; the Order AS IT STOOD IN MAY 2025 (between S 1031/2024 and the 2025
-- Revised Edition), which was not obtainable and is not deposited; the amending orders themselves. Para 4(2)(c) is taken on the
-- facts of one qualifying contract.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Central Provident Fund (Exemption) Order 2018 -- current version (from 1 June 2026)`

DECLARE `Residence status` IS ONE OF
    `a citizen of Singapore`
    `a permanent resident of Singapore`
    `neither a citizen nor a permanent resident`

GIVEN status IS A `Residence status`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a citizen or permanent resident` status IF
    NOT (status EQUALS `neither a citizen nor a permanent resident`)

§§ `The Schedule, paragraphs 6 to 9 -- students`

-- Sched para 6: "An employee who is a matriculated or registered student of any of the following institutions and employed for
-- training approved by the institution concerned: (a) any university whose function of providing university education is
-- determined by any written law; (b) the Institute of Technical Education, Singapore ...; (c) a polytechnic established by any
-- written law; (d) a school specified in Part II or III of the Schedule to the [Edusave Pupils Fund] Regulations (Rg 1);
-- (e) Mountbatten Vocational School."
GIVEN s IS A Student
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is specified in Schedule paragraph 6` s IF
        s's `matriculated or registered`
    AND `is a paragraph 5 institution` (s's `institution`)
    AND s's `employed for training approved by the institution`

GIVEN s IS A Student
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is specified in Schedule paragraph 6(a)` s IF
        `is specified in Schedule paragraph 6` s
    AND s's `institution` EQUALS `a university whose function is determined by written law`

-- Sched para 7: "(a) a matriculated or registered student of any private education institution; (b) enrolled in a full-time
-- programme offered by the private education institution, that is subsidised by the Ministry of Education and listed on the
-- Ministry's website; and (c) employed for training approved by the private education institution."
GIVEN s IS A Student
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is specified in Schedule paragraph 7` s IF
        s's `matriculated or registered`
    AND s's `institution` EQUALS `a private education institution`
    AND s's `in a full-time MOE-subsidised programme listed on the MOE website`
    AND s's `employed for training approved by the institution`

-- Sched para 8: "(a) is a matriculated or registered student of any overseas tertiary education institution; (b) is required by
-- the overseas tertiary education institution to undergo training in Singapore for a period of not more than 6 months; and
-- (c) submits to his or her employer a written confirmation from the overseas tertiary education institution ..."
GIVEN s IS A Student
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is specified in Schedule paragraph 8` s IF
        s's `matriculated or registered`
    AND s's `institution` EQUALS `an overseas tertiary education institution`
    AND s's `required by the institution to train in Singapore for months` GREATER THAN 0
    AND s's `required by the institution to train in Singapore for months` AT MOST 6
    AND s's `gave the employer the institution's written confirmation`

-- Sched para 9: "An employee who is a registered student (other than a student who has completed the GCE 'A' Level Examination or
-- its equivalent) of any of the following institutions and employed during a school holiday period: (a) a Government school
-- ... (j) Madrasah Wak Tanjong Al-Islamiah."
GIVEN s IS A Student
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is specified in Schedule paragraph 9` s IF
        s's `matriculated or registered`
    AND s's `institution` EQUALS `a school listed in paragraph 8`
    AND (NOT s's `has completed the GCE A Level or equivalent`)
    AND s's `employed during a school holiday period`

GIVEN s IS A Student
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a student specified in the current Schedule` s IF
       `is specified in Schedule paragraph 6` s
    OR `is specified in Schedule paragraph 7` s
    OR `is specified in Schedule paragraph 8` s
    OR `is specified in Schedule paragraph 9` s

§§ `The Schedule, paragraphs 2, 2A and 3 -- international organisations`

-- Sched para 2: "An employee of the United Nations Organisation, or any agency, institution or related organisation of the United
-- Nations Organisation that is located in Singapore." [S 895/2025 wef 31/12/2025]
-- Sched para 2A: "An employee of any of the following entities, which is part of the World Bank Group ..., that is located in
-- Singapore: (a) the International Centre for Settlement of Investment Disputes; (b) the Multilateral Investment Guarantee
-- Agency." [S 895/2025 wef 31/12/2025]
-- Sched para 3: "An employee of the Organisation for Economic Co-operation and Development who is assigned to work for the
-- International Energy Agency Regional Cooperation Centre that is located in Singapore."
DECLARE `Schedule employer` IS ONE OF
    `the UN or a UN agency, institution or related organisation located in Singapore`
    `the International Centre for Settlement of Investment Disputes, located in Singapore`
    `the Multilateral Investment Guarantee Agency, located in Singapore`
    `the OECD, assigning the employee to the IEA Regional Cooperation Centre in Singapore`
    `the OECD, on other work`
    `any other employer`

GIVEN e IS A `Schedule employer`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is specified in Schedule paragraph 2, 2A or 3` e IF
       e EQUALS `the UN or a UN agency, institution or related organisation located in Singapore`
    OR e EQUALS `the International Centre for Settlement of Investment Disputes, located in Singapore`
    OR e EQUALS `the Multilateral Investment Guarantee Agency, located in Singapore`
    OR e EQUALS `the OECD, assigning the employee to the IEA Regional Cooperation Centre in Singapore`

§§ `Paragraph 4 -- domestic employees (transitional, from 1 June 2026)`

-- Para 4(1): Y "is exempt from paying [s 7 and community-fund contributions] in respect of wages payable to X under the current
-- contract for any month after 31 May 2026 if, in every period of 7 consecutive days falling within that month, X's domestic
-- employment by Y under the current contract does not exceed 14 hours".
-- Para 4(2): "(a) X is a citizen or permanent resident of Singapore; (b) either or both of the following contracts were entered
-- into before 1 June 2026: (i) the current contract; (ii) a domestic employment contract between X and Y that is a prior
-- connected contract ...; and (c) X's domestic employment under at least one of the contracts that satisfies sub-paragraph (b)
-- -- (i) started before 1 June 2026; and (ii) does not exceed 14 hours -- (A) where the domestic employment started on or after
-- 25 May 2026 -- in the period beginning on the date on which the domestic employment starts and ending on 31 May 2026 ...; or
-- (B) where the domestic employment started before 25 May 2026 -- in every period of 7 consecutive days falling within any one
-- calendar month of the period beginning on the date on which the domestic employment starts and ending on 31 May 2026".
-- (B) is taken as an input in its own words: whether "any one calendar month" means some month or every month is a fork (NOTES).
DECLARE `Domestic engagement` HAS
    `X is a domestic employee of Y` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the current contract or a prior connected contract was entered into before 1 June 2026` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employment under that contract started before 1 June 2026` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employment under that contract started on or after 25 May 2026` IS A BOOLEAN
    `hours worked from the start to 31 May 2026` IS A NUMBER
    `within any one calendar month to 31 May 2026, no 7 consecutive days exceeded 14 hours` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the month is after 31 May 2026` IS A BOOLEAN
    `most hours in any 7 consecutive days within the month` IS A NUMBER

-- Para 4(3): contract A is a "prior connected contract" if "(a) contract A is a prior contract in relation to the current
-- contract; and (b) either or both of the following apply: (i) X's domestic employment by Y under the current contract starts not
-- more than one month after the expiry or termination of contract A; (ii) between [then and the start of the current contract],
-- X is employed by Y under one or more other prior contracts ... without any continuous break of more than one month".
-- Para 5(3) defines the same term for seamen in the same words.
GIVEN `contract A is a prior contract` IS A BOOLEAN, `months from the end of contract A to the start of the current contract` IS A NUMBER, `employed by Y in between under other prior contracts with no break over one month` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `contract A is a prior connected contract` `contract A is a prior contract` `months from the end of contract A to the start of the current contract` `employed by Y in between under other prior contracts with no break over one month` IF
        `contract A is a prior contract`
    AND (    `months from the end of contract A to the start of the current contract` AT MOST 1
          OR `employed by Y in between under other prior contracts with no break over one month`)

GIVEN d IS A `Domestic engagement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the hours before June 2026 did not exceed 14` d IF
    IF d's `the employment under that contract started on or after 25 May 2026`
    THEN d's `hours worked from the start to 31 May 2026` AT MOST 14
    ELSE d's `within any one calendar month to 31 May 2026, no 7 consecutive days exceeded 14 hours`

GIVEN status IS A `Residence status`, d IS A `Domestic engagement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `paragraph 4 exempts the employer` status d IF
        d's `X is a domestic employee of Y`
    AND `is a citizen or permanent resident` status
    AND d's `the current contract or a prior connected contract was entered into before 1 June 2026`
    AND d's `the employment under that contract started before 1 June 2026`
    AND `the hours before June 2026 did not exceed 14` d
    AND d's `the month is after 31 May 2026`
    AND d's `most hours in any 7 consecutive days within the month` AT MOST 14

§§ `Paragraph 5 -- seamen (transitional, from 1 June 2026)`

-- Para 5(1): Y "is exempt from paying [s 7 and community-fund contributions] in respect of wages payable to X under the current
-- contract for any period after 31 May 2026". Para 5(2): "(a) X is a citizen of Singapore; (b) either or both of [the current
-- contract or a prior connected contract] were entered into before 1 June 2026 ...; and (c) X's employment under at least one of
-- the contracts that satisfies sub-paragraph (b) started before 1 June 2026."
-- Para 5(4): "seaman contract" means a contract under which an individual is employed as a seaman "(a) in a Swedish ship on terms
-- and conditions of service applicable to Swedish seamen; (b) in a Norwegian ship on [Norwegian terms]; or (c) by the East
-- Asiatic Co. Ltd. of Denmark on terms and conditions of the agreement between the Danish Shipowners' Association and the
-- Seamen's Union in Denmark."
DECLARE `Seaman contract kind` IS ONE OF
    `in a Swedish ship on Swedish seamen's terms`
    `in a Norwegian ship on Norwegian seamen's terms`
    `by the East Asiatic Co Ltd of Denmark on the Danish agreement terms`
    `not a seaman contract`

DECLARE `Seaman engagement` HAS
    `kind of contract` IS A `Seaman contract kind`
    `the current contract or a prior connected contract was entered into before 1 June 2026` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employment under that contract started before 1 June 2026` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the period is after 31 May 2026` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN status IS A `Residence status`, m IS A `Seaman engagement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `paragraph 5 exempts the employer` status m IF
        (NOT (m's `kind of contract` EQUALS `not a seaman contract`))
    AND status EQUALS `a citizen of Singapore`
    AND m's `the current contract or a prior connected contract was entered into before 1 June 2026`
    AND m's `the employment under that contract started before 1 June 2026`
    AND m's `the period is after 31 May 2026`

§§ `Paragraphs 2, 3 and 3A -- the exemptions`

-- Para 2(1): "An employer whose employee is specified in the Schedule (other than an employee specified in paragraph 6(a) of the
-- Schedule) is exempt from paying the following contributions in respect of wages payable to that employee: (a) any contribution
-- to the Fund under section 7 of the Act; (b) any contribution to a fund for the educational, social or economic advancement of
-- any community approved by the Minister for the purposes of section 76(3) of the Act."
-- Para 2(2): "An employer whose employee is specified in paragraph 6(a) of the Schedule is exempt from paying the contributions
-- mentioned in sub-paragraph (1)(a) and (b) in respect of wages payable to that employee."
-- Para 3: "An employer is exempt from paying any contribution to the Fund under section 7 of the Act in respect of wages payable to
-- an employee who is not a citizen or permanent resident of Singapore."
-- Para 3A: "A platform operator is exempt from paying any contribution to the Fund under section 8A of the Act in respect of
-- platform remuneration payable to a platform worker who is not a citizen or permanent resident of Singapore."
GIVEN student IS A Student, employer IS A `Schedule employer`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is specified in the current Schedule` student employer IF
       `is a student specified in the current Schedule` student
    OR `is specified in Schedule paragraph 2, 2A or 3` employer

GIVEN student IS A Student, employer IS A `Schedule employer`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `paragraph 2(1) exempts the employer` student employer IF
        `is specified in the current Schedule` student employer
    AND (NOT `is specified in Schedule paragraph 6(a)` student)

GIVEN student IS A Student
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `paragraph 2(2) exempts the employer` student IF `is specified in Schedule paragraph 6(a)` student

GIVEN status IS A `Residence status`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `paragraph 3 exempts the employer` status IF NOT `is a citizen or permanent resident` status

GIVEN status IS A `Residence status`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `paragraph 3A exempts the platform operator from section 8A contributions` status IF
    NOT `is a citizen or permanent resident` status

GIVEN status IS A `Residence status`, student IS A Student, employer IS A `Schedule employer`, d IS A `Domestic engagement`, m IS A `Seaman engagement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `today the employer is exempt from section 7 contributions` status student employer d m IF
       `paragraph 2(2) exempts the employer` student
    OR `paragraph 2(1) exempts the employer` student employer
    OR `paragraph 3 exempts the employer` status
    OR `paragraph 4 exempts the employer` status d
    OR `paragraph 5 exempts the employer` status m

-- Community-fund contributions (s 76(3)): paras 2(1)(b), 2(2), 4(1)(b) and 5(1)(b) exempt them; para 3 does not.
GIVEN status IS A `Residence status`, student IS A Student, employer IS A `Schedule employer`, d IS A `Domestic engagement`, m IS A `Seaman engagement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `today the employer is exempt from community-fund contributions` status student employer d m IF
       `paragraph 2(2) exempts the employer` student
    OR `paragraph 2(1) exempts the employer` student employer
    OR `paragraph 4 exempts the employer` status d
    OR `paragraph 5 exempts the employer` status m

GIVEN status IS A `Residence status`, student IS A Student, employer IS A `Schedule employer`, d IS A `Domestic engagement`, m IS A `Seaman engagement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `today section 7 contributions are payable on the wages` status student employer d m IF
    NOT `today the employer is exempt from section 7 contributions` status student employer d m

-- Which paragraph exempts, taking 2(2), 2(1), 4, 5 and 3 in that order where more than one applies (the encoder's order; the
-- Order does not rank them, and the result is the same exemption from s 7 contributions).
GIVEN status IS A `Residence status`, student IS A Student, employer IS A `Schedule employer`, d IS A `Domestic engagement`, m IS A `Seaman engagement`
GIVETH A STRING
`the exempting paragraph` status student employer d m MEANS
    IF `paragraph 2(2) exempts the employer` student THEN "para 2(2)"
    ELSE IF `paragraph 2(1) exempts the employer` student employer THEN "para 2(1)"
         ELSE IF `paragraph 4 exempts the employer` status d THEN "para 4"
              ELSE IF `paragraph 5 exempts the employer` status m THEN "para 5"
                   ELSE IF `paragraph 3 exempts the employer` status THEN "para 3"
                        ELSE "none"
